# Google AdSense Implementation Summary

This document summarizes the steps taken to correctly implement Google AdSense for the site ownership verification and ad serving.

## 1. Environment Variable Setup
We utilize an environment variable to securely and dynamically manage the AdSense Publisher ID. 
- **Variable Name:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_PUBLISHER_ID`
- **Value:** `pub-7089675560767740` (Set in `.env`)

This approach ensures the Publisher ID can be updated in one place without modifying the codebase.

## 2. Layout Integration (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
The AdSense requirements have been integrated into the root layout to ensure they are present on every page of the application. 

### ID Normalization
The code automatically checks if the `NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_PUBLISHER_ID` has the `ca-` prefix required by Google's script and meta tags. If missing, it prepends it:
```typescript
let adsensePublisherId = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_PUBLISHER_ID || '';
if (adsensePublisherId && !adsensePublisherId.startsWith('ca-')) {
  adsensePublisherId = \`ca-\${adsensePublisherId}\`;
}
```

### Site Ownership Meta Tag
Google requires a specific meta tag in the `<head>` of the document to verify site ownership.
```tsx
<meta name="google-adsense-account" content={adsensePublisherId} />
```

### AdSense Script Tag
The core AdSense JavaScript snippet is injected using Next.js's native `<Script>` component to optimize loading performance.
```tsx
<Script
  async
  src={\`https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=\${adsensePublisherId}\`}
  crossOrigin="anonymous"
  strategy="afterInteractive"
/>
```

## 3. Publisher Authorization (`public/ads.txt`)
To authorize Google to sell ads on your site, an `ads.txt` file was created in the `public/` directory. This file is served at the root of the domain (e.g., `yoursite.com/ads.txt`).
- **Path:** `public/ads.txt`
- **Content:** `google.com, pub-7089675560767740, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0`

## Conclusion
With these three components configured—**meta tag**, **script snippet**, and **ads.txt**—Google AdSense will be able to successfully verify the site ownership and serve ads effectively across the application.
